+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396, which obsoletes RFC 7386) and returns the
+merged document. A non-object patch (including an array or `null`) replaces the target; an object patch merges
+member by member, recursively, with `null` removing a key. Because `null` means "remove", a merge patch cannot set
+a member to `null`. Neither argument is mutated, the result shares no structure with them, and `__proto__` keys are
+treated as ordinary members. It never throws.
