@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Spec: applyMergePatch
+
+**Standard**: JSON Merge Patch, RFC 7396 §2 (obsoletes RFC 7386, the number used in the request; the
+algorithm is the same). Constitution I names RFC 7396.
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` implements the §2 MergePatch algorithm:
+- a non-object patch (primitive, `null`, array) replaces the target wholesale;
+- an object patch applied to a non-object target (including an array) starts from `{}`;
+- a `null` member removes the key (absent key is a no-op); other members merge recursively.
+
+Arguments are never mutated and the result shares no structure with them. `__proto__` keys are set as own
+members, never through the prototype. Nulls nested in an object patch that lands on a missing member are dropped (§2 example:
+`{"a":{"bb":{"ccc":null}}}` applied to `{}` gives `{"a":{"bb":{}}}`).
